exercises.solution:
By Theorem 3, count partitions of $\{1, 2, 3, 4\}$ by block sizes:

- one block of $4$: $1$ way;
- $3 + 1$: choose the single element, $4$ ways;
- $2 + 2$: the block containing $1$ has one more element, $3$ ways;
- $2 + 1 + 1$: choose the pair, $6$ ways;
- $1 + 1 + 1 + 1$: $1$ way.

Total $1 + 4 + 3 + 6 + 1 = 15$, the Bell number $B_4$. The experiment in the lesson confirms this by checking all $1024$ symmetric relations on four elements.

